#134;, veterans Bob BROWN&#134;, Jim FARMER&#134;, tourist Shelby GALLOWAY&#134;- offer views on the war, Kerry & the Vietnam generation.]", "segment_duration": 260, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763478, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "1SY1K5Ig9t", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-21", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763477, "segment_id": "Umn06vPHSV", "segment_broadcast_id": "1SY1K5Ig9t", "segment_title": "Iraq / Al-Sadr Revolt / Najaf", "segment_description": "(Studio: Sharyl Attkisson)  Report introduced. \n (Baghdad: Barry Petersen)  The smoldering insurgency in Najaf, Iraq, featured; scenes shown from al-Bezergan&#134; of an oil pipeline on fire, from the streets of Najaf of the followers of Shiite cleric Muqtada al-Sadr & from Baghdad's Sadr City; details given about the fate of kidnapped American Micah Garen.  [Iraqi Council Ismael ZAYER&#134;- comments on the national fortune.]", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63300.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763479, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "1SY1K5Ig9t", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-21", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763477, "segment_id": "ALrw2It40a", "segment_broadcast_id": "1SY1K5